WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.275
Why do many animal parents care for their offspring?

00:00:03.275 --> 00:00:05.600
Their care helps the young survive.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:10.638
Baby animals may need food, a safe place and protection from danger.

00:00:10.638 --> 00:00:14.175
Parents do not care for babies to stop them from growing.

00:00:14.175 --> 00:00:18.162
Instead, their actions support growth and survival.

00:00:18.162 --> 00:00:22.812
Look for the purpose of a behavior, not only what the animal appears to be doing.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.488
A hungry chick needs food, not toys or rocks.

00:00:27.488 --> 00:00:30.638
Many parent birds bring food to their chicks.

00:00:30.638 --> 00:00:35.225
Other animals help their young find food, and some teach hunting skills.

00:00:35.225 --> 00:00:38.312
These are different ways to meet a similar need.

00:00:38.312 --> 00:00:46.075
When you answer a question about a hungry baby, connect the problem, hunger, with the helpful action, bringing or finding food.

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:49.412
Shelter is a safe place to live.

00:00:49.412 --> 00:00:52.038
A nest can provide shelter for young birds.

00:00:52.038 --> 00:00:55.788
A rabbit may dig a burrow, an underground shelter.

00:00:55.788 --> 00:00:59.738
Shelter is not something animals eat and not a sound they make.

00:00:59.738 --> 00:01:02.412
Different animals can use different kinds of shelter.

00:01:02.412 --> 00:01:09.162
Compare a nest and a burrow: they look different, but both can provide a protected place for young animals.

00:01:10.333 --> 00:01:13.783
Some animals live in groups that help protect their offspring.

00:01:13.783 --> 00:01:17.071
A lion parent can protect its cubs from danger.

00:01:17.071 --> 00:01:21.746
But we should not claim that every animal parent gives exactly the same care.

00:01:21.746 --> 00:01:27.933
Different animals have different behaviors, and some young receive little or no parental care.

00:01:27.933 --> 00:01:34.133
Your worksheet uses examples to show several ways that care can help young animals survive.

00:01:35.292 --> 00:01:37.817
Try using because in an explanation.

00:01:37.817 --> 00:01:40.929
A bird brings food because its chicks need nourishment.

00:01:40.929 --> 00:01:44.829
A nest provides shelter because it gives the young a place to stay.

00:01:44.829 --> 00:01:48.742
A parent protects its baby because danger can cause harm.

00:01:48.742 --> 00:01:54.379
In the activity you will complete sentences with food, shelter, protect and danger.

00:01:54.379 --> 00:01:57.642
Choose the word that fits the meaning of the whole sentence.
